it didn't take long for residents at  Desert Garden Condominiums to talk as  many are now left figuring out their  next move in fear that their condo will  soon be next on The Chopping Block  when I first moved over here  grass security two pools Wash House  Nursery  all kind of roses you can name that was  Perry Williams a resident for over 30  years describing how things used to look  at Desert Garden Condominiums and if  you've been around the property lately  it's not hard to tell it's been a ghost  town as tenants have been leaving left  and right with broken windows doors  tagged and tons of trash and debris and  empty lots the Desert Garden condos have  been operating for decades on the west  side of town but recently were purchased  by Ahern Rentals who decided to knock  them down for reasons unknown at this  time in my opinion looked at these  people as nothing we're not trying to  stop you from doing what you want to do  but just be fair about it if you want  the people to leave give them a fair way  out and those who have lived here for  years feel as if they're being pushed  out with demolition already in the works  many even offered money for their keys  Williams who lives on a fixed income  after retiring last year says if only he  had been told sooner but now he and his  wife are left with little to no options  all they had to do just tell me this was  going on I know I'm probably the only  one who's paying my rent six months in  advance I guarantee you but are you  moving I got to I got to uh be homeless  I don't want to be homeless  and we were told by Bartlett that Ahern  Rentals have provided an agency to help  relocate tenants but the process has  been less than helpful and we plan on  reaching out to the city tomorrow along  with the rental company to get more  information as to why desert Garden is  being torn down in The Newsroom Madison  Kimbrough 8 News Now
 

